#HELPS

0 PSIONICS~
Psionics are mental powers.  Each is its own command, practised with
Salir in the Astral Plane (WALKTO SALIR); nobody sells them.

  Assault   ego whip, torment, nightmare, mindblast
  Astral    astral walk, shift, project, telekinesis
  Defense   mindbar, psionic armor, psychic shield, transfusion
  Control   clairvoyance, confuse, mind leech, enervate, pyrotechnics

How you get them:
  - 2nd remort: one power from each discipline; 3rd: two each; 4th:
    three each; the 5th and final remort: all 17 psionic skills.
    Powers stack and return after each remort.
  - An immortal may grant powers, at once or with a later level.

A new or returned power starts at 1%.  Each opens at its own level and
below it can be neither used nor practised:

  17 psionic armor            21 confuse, enervate, nightmare, telekinesis
  18 clairvoyance, torment    22 mindbar, mind leech
  19 ego whip, project,       23 mindblast
     psychic shield           25 astral walk, shift
  20 pyrotechnics             28 transfusion

Type a power by its whole name or its short word: ASTRAL WALK or ASTRAL,
EGO WHIP or EGO, PSIONIC ARMOR or PSIONIC, MIND LEECH or MINDLEECH.  A
missed roll costs a little mana and no lag.

See also: REMORT, SALIR, PRACTICE
~

0 'ASTRAL WALK' ASTRAL~
Syntax: astral walk <character>
        astral <character>

Carries you, and your pet if it stands with you, to another character
anywhere in the world.  2.BOB picks the second Bob you can see.

  - Costs 70 mana, spent before the roll; finding no path costs nothing.
  - The target must be visible to you, not an immortal, not on NOSUMMON.
  - Their room must be one travel magic reaches: not no-recall, safe,
    private, jail, death trap, no-teleport, another class's guild hall,
    a newbie room past level 10, or past a Hyrule gate you have not
    earned.  It may take you out of a no-recall room, never into one.
  - A mind immune to mental attack cannot be reached; a resistant one
    may refuse you, and the mana is gone.
  - You arrive stunned until the next tick, unable to act.

Level 25 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, SHIFT, GATE, NOSUMMON
~

0 CLAIRVOYANCE~
Syntax: clairvoyance <character>

Shows you the room another character is in, anywhere in the world, as
LOOK would.  You do not move.

  - Costs 25 mana; usable in a fight.
  - Immortals cannot be scried.  A private, jail, death trap, gods-only,
    newbie or no-teleport room shows nothing ("They aren't here.").
  - Half the time the target feels watched.

Level 18 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, PROJECT, SCAN
~

0 CONFUSE~
Syntax: confuse [victim]

Confuses a victim (your foe if you name nobody).  Each round a confused
victim may wander in a daze instead of fighting until it shakes the
confusion off.

  - Costs your level plus 50 mana.
  - Lasts 4 ticks; 5 from level 30, 6 from level 40.
  - A mind immune to mental damage can never be confused, and a
    mentally resistant one may throw it off.
  - Somebody already confused, and the treasure goblin, are refused
    before anything is spent.

Level 21 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, NIGHTMARE, EGO WHIP
~

0 'EGO WHIP' EGOWHIP~
Syntax: ego whip [victim]
        ego [victim]

Lashes a victim's ego for mental damage that grows with your level,
halved by a saving throw.  In a fight it defaults to your foe.

  - Costs 20 mana.
  - A victim who fails the save also loses 2 STR, INT, WIS or DEX
    (chosen at random) for 4d5 ticks; one more point each at levels 15,
    25 and 35.  It does not stack.

Level 19 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, TORMENT, MINDBLAST
~

0 MINDBAR~
Syntax: mindbar
        mind bar

Walls your own mind: mental damage and mental drains against you are
halved.  It takes no target.

  - Costs 50 mana; lasts about a sixth of your level in ticks.
  - Cannot be combined with psionic armor or psychic shield.

Level 22 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, PSIONIC ARMOR, PSYCHIC SHIELD
~

0 MINDBLAST 'MIND BLAST'~
Syntax: mindblast
        mind blast

Strikes the mind of everybody in the room you could attack -- not your
group, pets, charmed followers, shopkeepers or immortals -- for mental
damage that grows with your level to level 50, halved by a saving throw.
The rest of the area feels only vertigo.

  - Costs 50 mana even when nobody is hit.

Level 23 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, EGO WHIP, TORMENT
~

0 'MIND LEECH' MINDLEECH~
Syntax: mind leech [victim]
        mindleech [victim]

Drains two to three times your level in mana from a victim (your foe if
you name nobody) and gives you half of what was taken.  A victim with no
mana takes mental damage instead.

  - Costs 30 mana.
  - A mind immune to mental attack gives nothing; a resistant one gives
    half.  Mindbar and other psionic defences reduce what is left.

Level 22 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, ENERVATE, MINDBAR
~

0 ENERVATE~
Syntax: enervate [victim]

Tears away a victim's movement and then their health, each from your
level to twice your level, and gives you half of what it took.  In a
fight it defaults to your foe.

  - Costs 35 mana.
  - A mind immune to mental attack gives nothing, a resistant one may
    lose only half, and psionic defences reduce the rest.

Level 21 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, MIND LEECH, TORMENT
~

0 NIGHTMARE~
Syntax: nightmare [victim]

Fills a victim's mind with horrors for a third of your level in ticks:
they regain no hit points, mana or movement, lose some mana at once, and
a mobile's armour worsens.  In a fight it defaults to your foe.

  - Costs 20 mana.  A victim who saves is unharmed, but the attempt still
    costs the mana and the wait and starts a fight.
  - Somebody already in a nightmare is refused.

Level 21 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, CURE NIGHTMARE, CONFUSE
~

0 PROJECT~
Syntax: project <direction>

Sends your spirit in a straight line in any of the ten directions while
your body stays put.  The spirit moves on by itself, showing each room
as LOOK would, for your level / 4 + 1 rooms, then returns.

  - Costs 25 mana.
  - It passes closed doors, and stops at a missing, secret or wizlocked
    exit or a room it may not enter.
  - Others may see a ghostly figure pass through.

Level 19 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, CLAIRVOYANCE, SCAN
~

0 'PSIONIC ARMOR' PSIONIC~
Syntax: psionic armor [character]
        psionic [character]

Armours a mind against mental attack, cutting mental damage by a quarter
for half your level in ticks.  With no name it armours you; otherwise
somebody in the room.

  - Costs 20 mana.
  - Cannot be combined with mindbar or psychic shield.

Level 17 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, MINDBAR, PSYCHIC SHIELD
~

0 'PSYCHIC SHIELD' PSYCHIC~
Syntax: psychic shield
        psychic

Shields every member of your group in the room who has no mental defence
yet, cutting mental damage by a quarter for half your level in ticks.

  - Costs 50 mana; must be used standing.
  - Does not replace mindbar, psionic armor or another psychic shield.

Level 19 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, PSIONIC ARMOR, MINDBAR
~

0 PYROTECHNICS~
Syntax: pyrotechnics [victim]

Ignites the air around a victim (your foe if you name nobody) for the
damage of a fireball cast at your level, halved by a saving throw.  It
may also heat a piece of the victim's equipment until it cannot be worn
for a while.

  - Costs 20 mana.  Unlike the other powers, a missed roll costs its
    wait as well as a little mana.  It does not consume a light source.

Level 20 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, FIRE SPELLS, HEAT METAL
~

0 SHIFT~
Syntax: shift <character>

Pulls another character to your room through a rift.  It does not move
you.

  - Costs 70 mana.  A mobile may resist, and the mana and wait are spent.
  - Refused, with nothing spent, for yourself, an immortal, somebody
    already here, an aggressive or summon-proof mobile, a player on
    NOSUMMON, when either of you is fighting, or when either of you is
    serving a jail sentence.
  - Your room must not be no-recall, teleport, river or arena, nor one
    you may not use magic from; theirs must be one travel magic reaches,
    and not safe or no-recall.
  - They must be able to enter your room by magic: not another class's
    guild, nor a guild hall whose guard would turn them away, nor -- for
    a mobile -- a room mobiles may not enter.
  - You are stunned until the next tick, so you cannot pull a victim in
    and strike first.

Level 25 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, ASTRAL WALK, SUMMON, NOSUMMON
~

0 TELEKINESIS TK~
Syntax: telekinesis <object>
        tk <object>

Fetches a visible, takeable object lying on the ground anywhere in the
world.  It takes the first by that name it can reach, which need not be
yours.

  - Costs 50 mana on success, a little on a miss.  If nothing it could
    fetch matches, you are told and it costs nothing.
  - It cannot fetch money, treasure, hidden containers, carried items,
    NOLOCATE items, or from protected or no-teleport rooms, and respects
    carry limits, ownership and quest binding.
  - A player's corpse you may loot comes from anywhere, a dungeon or a
    no-recall room included, whole, gear and all.

Level 21 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, LOCATE OBJECT
~

0 TORMENT~
Syntax: torment [victim]

Makes a victim relive old pain: mental damage from half your level to
three times your level, halved by a saving throw.  In a fight it
defaults to your foe.

  - Costs 20 mana.

Level 18 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, EGO WHIP, MINDBLAST
~

0 TRANSFUSION~
Syntax: transfusion <character>

Gives 50 of your own hit points to another character in the room, up to
their maximum.  You lose exactly 50 whatever they gain.

  - Costs 20 mana.  It cannot be used when doing so would reduce you
    to zero hit points.
  - Refuses yourself and anybody at full health.
  - Works in a fight, on anybody in the room.

Level 28 psionic power.

See also: PSIONICS, AID, HEALSPELL
~

-1 EXOTIC WEAPONS WEAPON WEAPONSMASTER AXE DAGGER FLAIL MACE POLEARM SPEAR SWORD
 WHIP~
Each weapon type has its own skill, and it decides how well you fight
with that weapon.  Any class may use any weapon.

  axe       axes, hand to great (not halberds)
  dagger    knives, daggers and other stabbing weapons
  flail     ball-and-chain weapons
  mace      clubs, hammers and maces
  polearm   pole weapons (not spears), halberds included
  spear     spears and staves
  sword     rapier to claymore
  whip      whips and chains
  exotic    strange magical weapons: cannot be bought, and is three
            times your level, up to 100%
  bow       see ARCHERY

Your class sets which weapon you start with and how well.  Rakar the
Weaponsmaster (WALKTO RAKAR) practises every weapon skill with anyone.
Knowing both your weapon and your foe's helps you PARRY.

See also: ARCHERY, PARRY, WEAPON MASTERY, WEAPON FLAGS
~

0 'WEAPON MASTERY' MASTERY WEAPONSMASTERY~
Weapon mastery belongs to warriors and thieves.  It cannot be learned or
practised: it grows by itself every level, to level 59.

Each blow with a wielded weapon adds a share of the weapon's own damage:

  - 4% a level in your own class's guild (236% at level 59);
  - 3% a level in any other guild or none (177% at level 59).

It is added before damroll.  A backstab, which has its own multiplier,
does not take it, and other classes and bare hands have none.

See also: WARRIOR, THIEF, GUILDS, WEAPONS
~

-1 AGGROSTAB~
Passive.  When an aggressive monster is about to attack you, you may get
the first strike instead.  A thief by class who knows BACKSTAB may open
with a backstab.

  - Sold by the thieves' guild only.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:30  Cleric:30  Thief:15  Warrior:24  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BACKSTAB, HIDE, STEALTH
~

0 BACKSTAB BS~
Syntax: backstab <victim>
        bs <victim>

Opens a fight with a blow from behind: your first two hits (three if
hasted) land with the backstab multiplier, which grows with your level
and is greater with a dagger.  A victim who is not awake takes double
and is always hit.

  - Needs a wielded weapon of any kind; not usable while fighting.
  - A victim below a third of their health is "hurt and suspicious".
  - Hit, miss or refusal: six seconds of lag.  It starts the fight.
  - A practised backstabber sometimes lands a FATALITY.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:20  Cleric:24  Thief:3  Warrior:14  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: FATALITY, HIDE, SNEAK, STEALTH
~

0 BASH~
Syntax: bash [victim]

Throws your weight into a foe to knock them down (your current foe if
you name nobody).  Weight carried, size, their dexterity against your
strength, and ten points a level of difference decide it.

  - A hit deals a little damage, costs the victim two rounds of lag
    (typed commands and special attacks, not ordinary blows), and you
    six seconds.
  - A miss puts you on the ground, resting, for nine seconds; you take
    more damage until you are struck back to your feet.
  - Riders, steeds and anybody already down cannot be bashed.
  - Dwarves are born holding bash at 1%.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:20  Cleric:5  Thief:15  Warrior:3  Monk:12  Necromancer:N/A

See also: TRIP, KICK, SHOVE, DIRT
~

0 BERSERK~
Syntax: berserk

A battle rage: you heal twice your level in hit points and gain a fifth
of your level in hitroll and damroll, but lose ten points of armour for
every five levels and use every other skill at half your level less.
Lasts about an eighth of your level in ticks.

  - Needs and costs 50 mana, and halves your movement; 3 seconds of lag.
  - A failure costs 25 mana, half your movement and 9 seconds of lag.
  - Easier when hurt or fighting.  Refused while calmed, berserk or
    frenzied.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:30  Cleric:29  Thief:35  Warrior:18  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: FRENZY, ENHANCED DAMAGE, BASH
~

0 'BLINDING FISTS'~
Syntax: blinding fists [victim]
        blinding [victim]

A monk's flurry of unarmed blows: four strikes, five from level 30 and
six from level 40, each landing for your level to three times your
level.  In a fight it defaults to your foe.  It does not blind.

  - Needs empty hands, 20 mana and 20 movement; costs 20 mana and 10
    movement.
  - Six seconds of lag, whether or not a blow lands.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:N/A  Warrior:N/A  Monk:20  Necromancer:N/A

See also: FISTS OF FURY, CRANE DANCE, NERVE DAMAGE
~

0 'CRANE DANCE' CRANE~
Syntax: crane dance
        crane

A monk's opening leap that strikes everybody in the room you could
attack.  Each foe loses about a quarter of its health if weak, a smaller
share the stronger it is, never more than 25 hit points per level of
yours.

  - Cannot be started once you are fighting; needs empty hands.
  - Needs 30 mana and a quarter of your maximum movement.  Costs 30 mana
    and half your movement (a quarter if it hits nobody).

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:N/A  Warrior:N/A  Monk:35  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BLINDING FISTS, FISTS OF FURY, IRON SKIN
~

0 'DANGER SENSE'~
Syntax: danger sense
        danger

Names the other players in your area you can see, and whether each is
nearby (five rooms or fewer), a little way off (twelve) or far away.  It
also counts players hidden by STEALTH or SHADOWMELD there.

  - Six seconds of lag.  Usable asleep at half your skill.
  - "You sense no danger" means nobody you can sense is about; a missed
    roll says you cannot tell what lies about you.
  - Sold by the warriors' guild only.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:36  Cleric:36  Thief:31  Warrior:13  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: TRACK, WHERE, SCAN
~

0 DESPAIR~
Passive.  Despair: when you try to FLEE, there is a chance (your skill
percentage) that your opponent loses heart and flees instead, leaving you
where you stand.  Hyrule's creatures are never driven off this way.

  - Every class, from level 25.  Rakar the Weaponsmaster sells it.

See also: FLEE, WIMPY, BERSERK
~

-1 DESTRUCTION~
Passive.  Your blows sometimes shatter your opponent's weapon.  The
chance is small.

  - Full warriors (warrior class in the warriors' guild) only.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:N/A  Warrior:26  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DISARM, SMITE, BASH
~

0 DIRT 'DIRT KICKING' DIRT-KICK~
Syntax: dirt kicking [victim]
        dirt [victim]

Kicks dirt in a foe's eyes (your current foe if you name nobody).  A hit
deals a little damage and blinds them, -4 to hit, until the next tick.

  - Your dexterity against twice theirs, speed and level decide it.
  - Easier in a desert or field, harder indoors, in a city or on a
    mountain, impossible on water or in the air.
  - Somebody already blind is refused.  Six seconds of lag either way.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:15  Cleric:15  Thief:6  Warrior:8  Monk:20  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BLINDNESS, BASH, TRIP
~

0 DISARM~
Syntax: disarm

Tries to knock the weapon from your current foe's hand; it takes no
name.  Your skill with both weapons, your dexterity against their
strength, and level decide it.

  - Needs a weapon or hand to hand.  Six seconds of lag either way.
  - A disarmed weapon falls to the floor, or into its owner's pack if it
    cannot be dropped.  BEWITCH WEAPON and HEROIC GRIP resist it.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:18  Cleric:17  Thief:16  Warrior:12  Monk:16  Necromancer:N/A

See also: HEROIC GRIP, BEWITCH WEAPON, BASH
~

-1 DODGE~
Passive.  A chance to step aside from a blow so it misses entirely.  Your
dexterity and the attacker's count.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:19  Cleric:22  Thief:5  Warrior:13  Monk:5  Necromancer:23

See also: PARRY, SHIELD BLOCK
~

-1 'ENHANCED DAMAGE'~
Passive.  A chance on each hit to deal extra damage; the better your
skill, the more often.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:31  Cleric:31  Thief:30  Warrior:16  Monk:14  Necromancer:N/A

See also: SECOND ATTACK, THIRD ATTACK, BERSERK
~

-1 FATALITY~
Passive.  Each BACKSTAB has a small chance to kill outright.  Full
thieves (thief class in the thieves' guild) only.

  - One percent for every 20% of skill, one more for dexterity above 22
    and another above 24, and three more against a monster ten or more
    levels below you.  Halved against a player, doubled against a
    sleeper: 5 to 10 percent at 100%.
  - Never against a higher-level victim, the training dummy, the
    treasure goblin, Ganon or Gohma.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:26  Warrior:N/A  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BACKSTAB, DESTRUCTION
~

0 'FISTS OF FURY' FISTS~
Syntax: fists of fury [victim]
        fists [victim]

A monk's fury of unarmed blows: two to five strikes, one more from level
35 and another from 45, each for your level to twice your level.  A
missed strike ends the fury and makes the victim try to flee.  In a
fight it defaults to your foe.

  - Needs empty hands; needs and costs 30 mana and 15 movement.
  - Six seconds of lag, whether or not a blow lands.
  - Hyrule's creatures will not be driven off; a miss just ends it.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:N/A  Warrior:N/A  Monk:30  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BLINDING FISTS, CRANE DANCE, STUNNING BLOW
~

-1 'HAND TO HAND'~
Passive.  Your fists are your weapon when you wield none, and hand to
hand lets you PARRY without a weapon (a parried blow is reduced rather
than stopped).  Monks are best at it.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:15  Warrior:6  Monk:1  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DISARM, SECOND ATTACK, PARRY
~

0 'IRON SKIN' IRON~
Syntax: iron skin
        iron

A monk hardens their own skin: armour class improves by 15 plus a fifth
of your level for one or two ticks.  Three times in four you are also
immune to one kind of weapon -- blunt, piercing or slashing -- and told
which; AFFECTS shows it.

  - Not in a fight; yourself only.
  - Costs 45 mana; a failure costs a few.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:N/A  Warrior:N/A  Monk:22  Necromancer:N/A

See also: STEEL FIST, CRANE DANCE, BLINDING FISTS
~

0 KICK~
Syntax: kick

Kicks your current foe for one to your level in damage.  It takes no
name and needs a fight.  Three seconds of lag either way.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:16  Cleric:12  Thief:14  Warrior:4  Monk:3  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BASH, TRIP, DIRT
~

0 LEVITATE~
Syntax: levitate

A monk's float: you fly for a tenth of your level in ticks, over water
and through the air like the FLY spell.

  - It always works, costs 10 mana and no lag.
  - Refused if you are already airborne.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:N/A  Warrior:N/A  Monk:13  Necromancer:N/A

See also: FLY, PSIONICS
~

0 'NERVE DAMAGE'~
Syntax: nerve damage [victim]
        nerve [victim]

A monk's jab at a nerve: (your level / 3) d10 damage, and for 3d3+3
ticks the victim loses 3 DEX and regains no hit points, mana or movement.
In a fight it defaults to your foe.  Monks start with it.

  - Needs empty hands, 20 mana and 10 movement.
  - A hit costs 15 mana and 10 movement, with lag.
  - A miss still deals 4d4 damage for 10 mana and 5 movement, no lag.
  - Hitting an already-affected victim does not renew the effect.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:N/A  Warrior:N/A  Monk:15  Necromancer:N/A

See also: STUNNING BLOW, BLINDING FISTS
~

-1 PARRY~
Passive.  A chance to turn a blow aside with your weapon.  Without a
weapon, hand to hand parries too, but only reduces the blow.  Knowing
both your weapon and your attacker's improves the chance.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:22  Cleric:20  Thief:13  Warrior:8  Monk:9  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DODGE, SHIELD BLOCK, HAND TO HAND
~

0 RESCUE~
Syntax: rescue <character>

Steps between a group member and whatever is fighting them, so it fights
you instead.

  - Only a player in your group who is fighting; pets and mobiles do not
    need it, and somebody you are fighting is "too late".
  - Your skill alone decides it.  Three seconds of lag either way.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:26  Cleric:20  Thief:18  Warrior:7  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: GROUP, FLEE, BASH
~

-1 'SLEIGHT OF HAND'~
Passive.  When you pick something up or take it from a container, a
chance that nobody in the room notices.  Sold by the thieves' guild.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:10  Cleric:18  Thief:6  Warrior:15  Monk:20  Necromancer:N/A

See also: STEAL, PEEK, PICK LOCK
~

0 STEAL~
Syntax: steal <object> <character>
        steal platinum|gold|silver|copper <character>

Takes something from another's pack, or up to a tenth of one pile of
their coin.

  - Not worn things, nor anything that cannot be dropped, is above your
    level, or that you could not carry.
  - The victim must not be fighting; a sleeper is far easier.  Anybody
    more than five levels above you is too wary.  Your chance tops out
    at 85%.
  - Six seconds of lag either way.  Not usable in STEALTH.
  - Fail and the victim cries out: a mobile attacks, and a player makes
    you WANTED.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:11  Cleric:11  Thief:8  Warrior:10  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: PEEK, HIDE, PKILL
~

0 STEALTH~
Syntax: stealth

A full thief's art: nobody without holylight or the Triforce can see you
at all -- not in the room, not by DETECT HIDDEN, not by WHERE -- for 12
ticks.

  - A success halves your current movement points; a failure costs
    nothing.  Metal armour cuts the chance to a third.
  - Refused while you are sneaking or hiding, and for two ticks after a
    fight with a player.  Striking anybody, or VISIBLE, ends it.
  - You cannot STEAL in stealth.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:18  Warrior:N/A  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: HIDE, SNEAK, SHADOWMELD, VISIBLE
~

0 'STEEL FIST' STEEL STEELFIST~
Syntax: steel fist
        steel

A monk hardens their hands: damroll rises by 3d3 plus a sixth of your
level for 5 to 8 ticks.

  - Not in a fight; empty hands; yourself only.
  - Costs 15 mana; a failure costs a few.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:N/A  Warrior:N/A  Monk:25  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BLINDING FISTS, FISTS OF FURY, IRON SKIN
~

0 'STUNNING BLOW'~
Syntax: stunning blow [victim]
        stunning [victim]

A monk's precise strike.  Your skill, your level against theirs, and
luck decide whether it stuns.  In a fight it defaults to your foe.

  - Needs empty hands; needs and costs 15 mana and 5 movement.
  - Stunned: the victim takes your level to three times your level, and
    on its next round of blows may lose the round while it recovers.
  - Missed: a glancing blow, half your level to your level -- never more
    than the weakest stunning one.
  - Either way the victim loses a round of command lag, and you lag too.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:N/A  Warrior:N/A  Monk:21  Necromancer:N/A

See also: NERVE DAMAGE, BASH, KICK
~

0 TRIP~
Syntax: trip [victim]

Takes a foe's feet from under them (your current foe if you name
nobody).  Size, their dexterity and speed, level and a little bad luck
count against you.

  - A hit deals a little damage, costs the victim a round of lag (typed
    commands and special attacks, not ordinary blows), and you six
    seconds; a miss costs you four.  Tripping yourself costs twelve.
  - Flying victims, riders, steeds and anybody already down cannot be
    tripped.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:21  Cleric:19  Thief:1  Warrior:15  Monk:10  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BASH, KICK, DIRT
~

-1 'SECOND ATTACK'~
Passive.  A chance at an extra blow each round.  Even at 100% it does
not guarantee one.  The warriors' guild gives it free.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:24  Cleric:22  Thief:12  Warrior:5  Monk:8  Necromancer:N/A

See also: THIRD ATTACK, DUAL WIELD
~

0 'FOURTH ATTACK'~
There is no fourth attack.  THIRD ATTACK is the last extra strike a
character can train; haste, dual wield and your weapon's speed supply
the rest of a round's blows.

See also: THIRD ATTACK, DUAL WIELD, HASTE
~

-1 'THIRD ATTACK'~
Passive.  A chance at a third blow each round, and a better chance at a
second.  Full warriors (warrior class in the warriors' guild) only.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:N/A  Warrior:15  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: SECOND ATTACK, DUAL WIELD
~

0 TRACK~
Syntax: track <character>

Tells you which way to go to reach somebody you can see anywhere in the
world, and whether they are just beyond, not far (five rooms or fewer),
some way off (fifteen or fewer) or a long way off.  It does not move you;
follow it and track again.  A missed roll says the trail was lost.

  - Follows the six ordinary directions only -- no diagonals or portals
    -- and not through the sky or deep water unless you fly.
  - Costs 3 movement points and a moment's lag; refused at 2 or fewer.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:25  Warrior:N/A  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: SCAN, WHERE, DANGER SENSE
~

-1 'FAST HEALING'~
Passive.  Improves how fast you regain hit points each tick, walking,
resting or sleeping.  It can fail on any tick.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:15  Cleric:14  Thief:16  Warrior:11  Monk:18  Necromancer:N/A

See also: MEDITATION, TICK
~

-1 HAGGLE HAGGLING~
Passive.  A chance to buy for less and sell for more in shops.  A
haggled sale never pays above what an item is worth.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:7  Cleric:18  Thief:1  Warrior:14  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: SLEIGHT OF HAND, BUY, SELL
~

0 HIDE~
Syntax: hide

Slips you into the shadows: you vanish from the room's list for anybody
without DETECT HIDDEN, holylight or the Triforce.  It says whether it
worked.

  - Takes no time and costs nothing.  Not in a fight.
  - Any command you type brings you out again; hiding is for waiting.
    To move unseen, see SNEAK and STEALTH.
  - Hobbits are born holding it.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:10  Cleric:16  Thief:2  Warrior:12  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: SNEAK, STEALTH, DETECT HIDDEN, BACKSTAB
~

0 SNEAK~
Syntax: sneak

Moves you quietly: while it lasts, rooms you enter and leave are not
told.  A success lasts your level in ticks.

  - Takes no time, costs nothing, and does not say whether it worked.
  - Wearing metal armour cuts the chance to a third; putting it on while
    sneaking rolls again at that third.  Not usable in STEALTH.
  - Elves are born holding it.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:8  Cleric:12  Thief:4  Warrior:10  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:7

See also: HIDE, STEALTH, BACKSTAB
~

0 'LISTEN AT DOOR'~
Syntax: listen <direction>

Listens through a closed door for anybody moving on the other side.  Any
of the ten directions, shortened or whole.

  - The exit must be a closed door you can see (not a secret one).
  - "You hear someone, or something" means somebody is there.  "Hear
    nothing on the other side" means nobody.  A missed roll says you
    cannot make anything out, and tells you nothing either way.
  - No cost and no lag.  Sold by the thieves' guild only.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:35  Cleric:35  Thief:17  Warrior:27  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: PEEK, SEARCH, PICK LOCK
~

0 LORE~
Syntax: lore <object>

Researches something you carry: type, weight, worth, armour or weapon
dice, affects, and the spells in potions, scrolls, pills, wands and
staves.  Every number is an estimate, half to double the truth.

  - Nine seconds of lag.
  - Costs gold: twenty times the object's level, less twice your skill
    and half your level, possibly to zero for simple items.
  - An object that cannot be identified says only that it is magical.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:5  Cleric:6  Thief:12  Warrior:20  Monk:25  Necromancer:N/A

See also: IDENTIFY, COMPARE, LOCATE OBJECT
~

-1 MEDITATION~
Passive.  Improves how fast you regain mana while resting or sleeping.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:6  Cleric:6  Thief:15  Warrior:15  Monk:9  Necromancer:8

See also: FAST HEALING, TICK
~

-1 PEEK~
Passive.  When you LOOK at somebody, a chance to see what they carry as
well.  Sold by the thieves' guild.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:21  Cleric:21  Thief:10  Warrior:14  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: STEAL, HIDE, SEARCH
~

0 PHASE~
Passive.  When you go to SLEEP, a chance (your skill percentage) that
you slip out of sight as though you had used STEALTH.

  - Every class, from level 25.  No trainer sells it.

See also: STEALTH, SHADOWMELD, SLEEP
~

0 PICK 'PICK LOCK'~
Syntax: pick lock <container>
        pick <container>
        pick <direction>

Opens a lock without its key.  A direction may be shortened (PICK WES).

  - Three seconds of lag before anything else, refusals included.
  - Not in a fight, nor with an awake mobile more than five levels above
    you in the room.
  - A lock beyond any pick, a magical lock, a keyless one, or something
    not closed or not locked is refused with the reason.  A fumble is a
    missed roll on a lock that can open: try again.
  - A trapped lock goes off when you succeed and stays locked; SEARCH
    first.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:23  Cleric:23  Thief:7  Warrior:25  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: SEARCH, UNLOCK, DOORBASH, OPEN
~

0 RIDE RIDING MOUNT DISMOUNT~
Syntax: ride <creature>
        mount <creature>
        dismount

Rides a mountable creature, which then pays the movement.

  - You need a saddle, carried or already on the creature.
  - The creature must not be fighting, following anyone or ridden, and
    you cannot keep a pet and a mount at once.
  - A failure throws you for 25 hit points; the chance tops out at 90%.
  - A mount cannot go indoors, into a law room, through a closed or
    secret exit, or into another class's guild.  The sky needs a flyer;
    deep water a flyer or swimmer.
  - Your mount, wearing its saddle, is saved with you when you quit, if it
    is beside you.  You come back dismounted, the mount saddled at your
    side; RIDE it again, with no saddle needed in your pack.  A mount you
    DISMOUNT is let go: it is not yours any more, and is not saved.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:6  Cleric:6  Thief:5  Warrior:4  Monk:5  Necromancer:6

See also: FLY, BASH, FOLLOW
~

0 SEARCH~
Syntax: search <container>
        search <direction>

Looks for a trap on a closed, locked container or door, and disarms it.

  - Costs six seconds of lag whatever happens, once you know the skill
    above 1%; below that it is refused, with no lag.
  - An awake mobile more than five levels above you stops you.
  - Success removes the trap (from both sides of a door) or says there
    is none.  A missed roll says only that it might be trapped -- and
    half the time sets the trap off if there is one.
  - Something not a closed, locked container or door is refused.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:9  Cleric:11  Thief:7  Warrior:11  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: PICK LOCK, DETECT TRAPS, PEEK
~

0 SMITE~
Syntax: smite <victim>

A warrior's crushing round: every hit adds damage from the weapon's own
dice, scaled by your skill -- once, twice above level 30, three times
above level 50.  Best with a sword; an axe, flail or mace a little less;
other weapons get no bonus.  In a fight it strikes your current foe.

  - Needs a wielded weapon.  Six seconds of lag either way.
  - Now and then it wears your weapon down; a weapon worn to nothing
    breaks.  REPAIR it and it never will.
  - Full warriors (warrior class in the warriors' guild) only.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:N/A  Cleric:N/A  Thief:N/A  Warrior:10  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BASH, REPAIR, DESTRUCTION
~

-1 WANDS STAVES SCROLLS~
Skills for using magical items.  Without them you fail, and may destroy
the item.

  scrolls   reading scrolls (RECITE)
  staves    using staves (BRANDISH)
  wands     using wands (ZAP)

The mage guild gets wands and scrolls free, the cleric guild staves and
scrolls.  GAINLIST shows whether you can buy them.

For scrolls, minimum level by class:
Mage:3  Cleric:4  Thief:5  Warrior:9  Monk:15  Necromancer:3

For staves, minimum level by class:
Mage:5  Cleric:2  Thief:9  Warrior:9  Monk:34  Necromancer:7

For wands, minimum level by class:
Mage:2  Cleric:5  Thief:9  Warrior:9  Monk:33  Necromancer:6

See also: RECITE, BRANDISH, ZAP, LORE
~

-1 'SHIELD BLOCK' SHIELDBLOCK BLOCK~
Passive.  Parrying with a shield: a chance to stop a blow with the
shield you wear.  Without the skill a shield defends you poorly.  Flails
ignore shield blocks and whips get round them more easily.

Minimum level by class (GAINLIST shows who sells it):
Mage:17  Cleric:17  Thief:16  Warrior:2  Monk:15  Necromancer:20

See also: PARRY, DODGE
~

0 $~

